---
import Docs from '../../../layouts/Docs.astro'
import Callout from 'web-design-system/astro/marketing/Callout.astro'
import CodeBlock from 'web-design-system/astro/product/CodeBlock.astro'
import TableScroll from '../../../components/atoms/TableScroll.astro'

const toc = [
  { label: 'Build inputs', href: '#inputs' },
  { label: 'CI and smoke workflows', href: '#workflows' },
  { label: 'The clean-machine gate', href: '#gate' },
  { label: 'Artifact checks', href: '#artifacts' },
  { label: 'Signing and updates', href: '#signing' },
]

const commands = `direnv exec . cargo fmt --check
direnv exec . cargo clippy --workspace -- -D warnings
direnv exec . cargo test -p agent-harness
direnv exec . cargo test -p shepherd-core
direnv exec . cargo test -p shepherd
direnv exec . cargo test -p shepherd --test packaging
direnv exec . cargo test -p shepherd --test shell_scope
direnv exec . pnpm --dir apps/shepherd/ui run typecheck
direnv exec . pnpm --dir apps/shepherd/ui run test:e2e`

const workflows = [
  { name: 'shepherd-package-smoke.yml', what: 'Manually dispatched debug macOS and Ubuntu bundle builds on clean runners. Checks packaging config, the macOS minimum version and the Debian executable.' },
  { name: 'shepherd-terminal-smoke.yml', what: 'The two-launch terminal suite under Xvfb on Ubuntu 24.04; the macOS window suites cover focus, visibility and IME.' },
  { name: 'shepherd-adapter-smoke.yml', what: 'Self-hosted installed-agent probes for OpenCode, Claude ACP and native RPC adapters. Each feature is gated separately.' },
]
---

<Docs
  title="Release pipeline"
  description="What builds Shepherd, what the smoke workflows prove, and why the clean-machine release gate is still pending."
  toc={toc}
>
  <Callout tone="warning" title="Preflight is not a release">
    The package smoke workflows build debug bundles without launching the app. They do not replace
    the clean-machine macOS 13+ and Ubuntu 24.04+ gate. That gate has not been run.
  </Callout>

  <h2 id="inputs">Build inputs</h2>
  <p>
    The app build is a Tauri 2 bundle over the SolidJS UI and the Rust core. The macOS build sets a
    deployment target of 13.0. The package test is the guard that keeps the Tauri config, build
    script, CI workflow and this document from drifting apart.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock filename="terminal" code={commands} showLineNumbers={false} />
  <p>
    The release checklist also records the commit being released. A local target directory is not
    evidence for a release; use a fresh target or <code>CARGO_TARGET_DIR</code>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="workflows">CI and smoke workflows</h2>
  <TableScroll label="Shepherd smoke workflows">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Workflow</th><th>What it covers</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {workflows.map((entry) => (
          <tr><td><code>{entry.name}</code></td><td>{entry.what}</td></tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </TableScroll>
  <p>
    The package smoke is manually dispatched and builds debug bundles. It verifies the macOS
    <code>LSMinimumSystemVersion</code> and <code>minos</code> values, the Debian package contents and
    that the executable has no <code>/nix/store</code> dependency. It does not launch the app, add a
    project or exercise an agent.
  </p>

  <h2 id="gate">The clean-machine gate</h2>
  <p>
    The gate uses clean macOS 13+ and Ubuntu 24.04+ machines or VMs with the release commit, not a
    developer checkout. For each platform it:
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li>Installs with <code>pnpm install --frozen-lockfile</code> and removes the target directory.</li>
    <li>Builds the macOS app bundle or Ubuntu Debian package.</li>
    <li>Checks the minimum system version and confirms the artifact has no Nix store path.</li>
    <li>Installs the package and launches it under the desktop session.</li>
    <li>Adds a repository, starts a task, answers an approval and inspects the diff.</li>
    <li>Runs the terminal smoke, plus the platform input checks where claimed.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    The evidence table is still pending for both platforms. A green preflight does not fill it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="artifacts">Artifact checks</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>macOS: exactly the expected <code>.app</code>, <code>LSMinimumSystemVersion 13.0</code>, <code>minos 13.0</code>, no <code>/nix/store</code> entries.</li>
    <li>Ubuntu: exactly one <code>.deb</code>, <code>usr/bin/shepherd</code> present, no <code>/nix/store</code> dependency, WebKitGTK 2.44+ at launch.</li>
    <li>Record the artifact hash, exact OS and commit in the release evidence.</li>
    <li>An unsigned or unnotarized build is a failure, not a warning, once signing is required.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="signing">Signing and updates</h2>
  <p>
    Signing and notarization are human-gated and are not configured for an ordinary build. The
    release owner either configures them or explicitly accepts unsigned artifacts for a release. v1
    has no updater; a new build is a manual replacement. Windows packages and signed Windows
    installers are planned, not part of the current gate.
  </p>
  <p>
    The user-facing status is on <a href="/docs/users/releases">Releases</a>. The checklist lives at
    <code>apps/shepherd/docs/release-checklist.md</code>; keep it and the packaging test in sync when
    a build input changes.
  </p>
</Docs>
